IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pra-rules`

§ `Tests`

GIVEN k IS A `Pension class`, amt IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Increase position`
`for` k `on` amt MEANS `the increase position for` (`Pensioner` OF k, amt, Date 16 11 1967)

#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 30)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 18.16
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 33)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 23.89
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 36)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 21.79
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 42)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 21.79
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 40)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`for` `a weekly pensioner under s 3` `on` 30)'s `from` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 11 1967)
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 4` `on` 2291.67)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 437.5
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 4` `on` 2750)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 525
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 4` `on` 3062)'s `the increase` EQUALS JUST 525
#ASSERT (`for` `an annual pensioner under s 4` `on` 30)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`for` `the widow of a man whose pension rose under s 3` `on` 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 48.16
#ASSERT (`for` `the widow of a man whose pension rose under s 4` `on` 0)'s `the widow's pension` EQUALS JUST 2729.17
#ASSERT (`for` `the widow of a man whose pension rose under s 4` `on` 0)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`for` `none of these` `on` 30)'s `the increase` EQUALS NOTHING
